Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Palatini-Goldberg Bootstrap for Gravity in Momentum Space", "Title",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.994932452363154*^9, 
  3.994932500415036*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"f00586b6-d56d-49e4-a8a1-\
0959e976f4ff"],

Cell["\<\
This notebook reconstructs the Goldberg-Palatini action from the Noether \
identities (classical Ward identities) of prescribed gauge transformations in \
momentum space, using FeynCalc. It generates the kernel and projection bases, \
constructs the six identities, solves their coefficient constraints, and \
compares the first-order kernels with the literature.

Conventions: Lorentz indices and momenta are treated abstractly in Nd \
dimensions using FeynCalc. No explicit metric components are assigned. Nd is \
used because D is reserved in Mathematica. Index parentheses in the \
analytical formulas denote unnormalized symmetrization, A_(mn) = A_mn + A_nm. \
The basis construction uses normalized group averages. The Fourier convention \
is f(p) = Integrate[exp(i p.x) f(x), x], with inverse measure d^Nd p/(2 \
Pi)^Nd, so a derivative on a field carrying momentum p gives -i p. The \
coupling is set to kappa = 1; the full metric density is h^{mn} = eta^{mn} + \
phi^{mn}.

Code-to-paper notation: the h in names such as Khh, KhG and delh0p denotes \
the metric-density perturbation phi, not the full density h^{mn}. Khh, KhG, \
KGG and V correspond to K^{phi phi}, K^{phi G}, K^{GG} and K^{phi GG}. delh0p \
and delG0p represent D_{phi^0} and D_{G^0}; delh1pq and delG1pq represent the \
field-dependent maps D_{phi^1} and D_{G^1}. The coefficient lists cfehh, \
cfehG, cfeGG and cfev follow the displayed notebook basis order, which \
differs from the paper's order. basishG includes an explicit factor i; its \
coefficients are listed relative to that convention.

Run the active input cells in order in a fresh kernel with FeynCalc \
installed. The optional Nd = 4 Gram diagnostic is commented out; keep Nd \
symbolic for the main calculation. The final sections check the first-order \
kernels and export them for the separate xAct comparison with CLM.\
\>", "Text",
 CellTags->
  "NotebookOverview",ExpressionUUID->"19424312-1e2a-4c86-aabd-a9a791c2897c"],

