Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["2) The Action Ansatz", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"65760471-447b-4d6b-9872-378316f47872"],

Cell["\<\
With kappa = 1, S = S_2 + S_3, where
S_2 = Int_p [Khh(phi(-p), phi(p)) + KhG(phi(-p), G(p)) + KGG(G(-p), G(p))],
S_3 = Int_p Int_q V(phi(p+q), G(-p), G(-q)).
Each kernel denotes full contraction with its field arguments, and Int_p = \
integral d^Nd p/(2 Pi)^Nd. The quadratic kernels have momentum degrees 2, 1 \
and 0, respectively; V is momentum independent. The fields are symmetric in \
their two metric/lower-connection slots. No additional factorials are \
included in this kernel convention.

The local, parity-even ansatz restricts the cubic sector to phi G G. This is \
an input, not a consequence of dimensional counting alone. Its completion is \
tested through the six identities below.\
\>", "Text",
 CellTags->
  "ActionAnsatz",ExpressionUUID->"76d8a911-a827-4c8f-b71a-2f07f7b8db85"]
}, Open  ]],

