Cell[TextData[{
 "Both expressions are consistent with those in F. T. Brandt and D. G. C. \
McKeon, Radiative corrections and the Palatini action, arXiv:1601.04944, Eqs. \
(3.5)-(3.6). Again, however, we must fix coefficients by hand to obtain the \
desired relation. This is not merely a normalization choice: here the \
coefficients are fixed to eliminate certain parts of the kernel ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["K", "TI"], 
        RowBox[{
          StyleBox["h", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["G", "TI"]}]], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "K_{hG}", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "5b851af4-7c4e-4ab8-90a9-ba6b589b4259"],
 " and recover its known form. Once this is done, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["K", "TI"], 
         RowBox[{
           StyleBox["G", "TI"], 
           StyleBox["G", "TI"]}]], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
      "K_{GG}", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
     "TeXAssistantTemplate"], " "}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "a70702ed-ac68-4969-a929-13e1638be97b"],
 " is uniquely determined. "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9937280089619017`*^9, 3.993728150571898*^9}, {
  3.9937282220170727`*^9, 3.993728259189467*^9}, {3.9937283635241737`*^9, 
  3.993728381731983*^9}, {3.993728420063513*^9, 
  3.993728421309929*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"20debd52-39d1-4fb2-9888-\
8d3ba63b33e8"],

Cell["\<\
These by-hand choices serve only to compare with the literature at this \
stage. In the cubic chapter, no additional coefficient choices are imposed: \
within the prescribed ansatz, W31 forces Khh = 0 and W32 forces ahG = 0, so \
that the form of S_2 is fixed by the identities themselves.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ce3e6de2-947c-4fb5-9dce-9febce62251e"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

