Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Decomposition Bases", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.994947132469829*^9},ExpressionUUID->"faaca91e-d8dc-411f-91bd-\
c98c8ba743c8"],

Cell["\<\
We begin with equal external field momenta to simplify the projection bases. \
This specialization yields necessary conditions and may leave additional \
freedom. The specialized system below has a one-dimensional solution space, \
and the Goldberg-Palatini action is invariant for arbitrary momenta and \
belongs to it. Once that geometric identification is established, the full \
and specialized solution spaces coincide within the ansatz (Section IV of the \
paper).\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9949471382335157`*^9, 
  3.994947235736916*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"50bffb76-3584-4504-9f77-\
75dd04c485a5"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["W31:", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.993996533830758*^9, 3.993996541543837*^9}, {
  3.993999482243567*^9, 3.993999501302104*^9}, {3.994946753606491*^9, 
  3.9949467781653757`*^9}, {3.994947780013158*^9, 
  3.9949477807808123`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"1507cc9f-e15e-449b-83ea-\
7620a440c63e"],

Cell["\<\
If the cubic vertex contains only phi G G, the phi phi sector of delta^(1) \
S_2 + delta^(0) S_3 = 0 gives an identity involving Khh alone. The \
field-dependent transformation in the following formula is D_{phi^1}.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.993996552661304*^9, 3.993996568032193*^9}, 
   3.99399803306459*^9, {3.993999221147835*^9, 
   3.993999307969298*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"d502d6a4-0e62-4abe-8133-\
61dbcee27b16"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         SubsuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
          RowBox[{
            SubscriptBox["\[Mu]", "1"], 
            SubscriptBox["\[Nu]", "1"], 
            SubscriptBox["\[Mu]", "2"], 
            SubscriptBox["\[Nu]", "2"], "\[Rho]"}], "31"], 
         RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{
             SubscriptBox[
              StyleBox["p", "TI"], "1"], ",", 
             SubscriptBox[
              StyleBox["p", "TI"], "2"]}], ")"}], "\[LongEqual]", 
         SubsuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["K", "TI"], 
          RowBox[{
            SubscriptBox["\[Mu]", "1"], 
            SubscriptBox["\[Nu]", "1"], "\[Alpha]\[Beta]"}], 
          RowBox[{
            StyleBox["h", "TI"], 
            StyleBox["h", "TI"]}]], 
         RowBox[{"(", 
           SubscriptBox[
            StyleBox["p", "TI"], "1"], ")"}], 
         SubsuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
          RowBox[{
            SubscriptBox["\[Mu]", "2"], 
            SubscriptBox["\[Nu]", "2"], "\[Rho]"}], "\[Alpha]\[Beta]"], 
         RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{
             SubscriptBox[
              StyleBox["p", "TI"], "1"], ",", 
             SubscriptBox[
              StyleBox["p", "TI"], "1"], "+", 
             SubscriptBox[
              StyleBox["p", "TI"], "2"]}], ")"}], "+", 
         SubsuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["K", "TI"], 
          RowBox[{
            SubscriptBox["\[Mu]", "2"], 
            SubscriptBox["\[Nu]", "2"], "\[Alpha]\[Beta]"}], 
          RowBox[{
            StyleBox["h", "TI"], 
            StyleBox["h", "TI"]}]], 
         RowBox[{"(", 
           SubscriptBox[
            StyleBox["p", "TI"], "2"], ")"}], 
         SubsuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
          RowBox[{
            SubscriptBox["\[Mu]", "1"], 
            SubscriptBox["\[Nu]", "1"], "\[Rho]"}], "\[Alpha]\[Beta]"], 
         RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{
             SubscriptBox[
              StyleBox["p", "TI"], "2"], ",", 
             SubscriptBox[
              StyleBox["p", "TI"], "1"], "+", 
             SubscriptBox[
              StyleBox["p", "TI"], "2"]}], ")"}], "\[LongEqual]", "0"}], 
       TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "W^{31}_{\\mu_1 \\nu_1 \\mu_2 \\nu_2 \\rho} (p_1 , p_2 ) = \
K^{hh}_{\\mu_1 \\nu_1 \\alpha \\beta} (p_{1} ) D^{\\alpha \\beta}_{\\mu_2 \
\\nu_2 \\rho} (p_{1}, p_{1} + p_{2}) + K^{hh}_{\\mu_2 \\nu_2 \\alpha \\beta} \
(p_{2}) D^{\\alpha \\beta}_{\\mu_1 \\nu_1 \\rho} (p_{2},p_{1}+p_{2}) = 0", 
     "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "1a4eb70c-18b8-4ac9-b0e5-43bf847c1524"],
 "\n\nBelow we take p1 = p2 = p. Since the identities must hold for arbitrary \
momenta, this specialization can at worst yield no useful information; it \
cannot produce an incorrect necessary condition."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.993998864454567*^9, {3.993999313860387*^9, 3.993999390593923*^9}, 
   3.9939995216745567`*^9, {3.994004924489956*^9, 
   3.9940049249415913`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"1a3134a9-8d60-4d5f-9ee4-\
379209f7500a"],

