Cell["\<\
Here we use ahG and cGG as the free coefficients. In the displayed basishG \
order, ahG multiplies the first element, i/4 times p_(mu eta_nu)(rho \
eta_sigma)lambda, with unnormalized parentheses. After Khh = 0, this \
parametrizes the remaining relative freedom in the quadratic action; W32 sets \
ahG to zero. cGG then parametrizes the overall normalization. We store the \
results:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9957011372814417`*^9, 
  3.995701260246407*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"6b1b1d8e-26a8-40c4-9ac8-\
cb85237c0993"],

